The attached image (Fig. 6) demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the expression of costimulatory molecules CD80 and CD86 on dendritic cells (DCs), indicating their activation. Flow cytometry histograms show DCs incubated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) or medium control (gray line) for two days. Compared to the control, Nano-11 treatment resulted in a slight increase in CD40 expression but a marked upregulation of CD80 and CD86. This enhanced expression of costimulatory molecules is a crucial step in the initiation of an effective immune response, highlighting Nano-11's role as an immunostimulatory vaccine adjuvant.